Writing PostgreSQL migration. Splits `full_name` into `first_name` and `last_name`, handles re-runs, includes rollback.

```sql
-- migration_001_split_name.sql
-- UP: Split full_name into first_name and last_name

BEGIN;

-- 1. Check if already migrated (idempotent)
DO $$
BEGIN
  IF NOT EXISTS (
    SELECT 1 FROM information_schema.columns 
    WHERE table_name = 'users' AND column_name = 'first_name'
  ) THEN
    -- 2. Add new columns
    ALTER TABLE users ADD COLUMN first_name VARCHAR(255);
    ALTER TABLE users ADD COLUMN last_name VARCHAR(255);

    -- 3. Backfill from full_name (split on last space, or fallback)
    UPDATE users SET
      first_name = TRIM(SUBSTRING(full_name, 1, POSITION(' ' IN full_name) - 1)),
      last_name = TRIM(SUBSTRING(full_name, POSITION(' ' IN full_name) + 1))
    WHERE full_name LIKE '% %';

    -- 4. Handle single-word names (no space)
    UPDATE users SET
      first_name = TRIM(full_name),
      last_name = ''
    WHERE full_name NOT LIKE '% %' AND first_name IS NULL;

    -- 5. Set NOT NULL constraint
    ALTER TABLE users ALTER COLUMN first_name SET NOT NULL DEFAULT '';
    ALTER TABLE users ALTER COLUMN last_name SET NOT NULL DEFAULT '';

    -- 6. Optional: keep full_name as generated column (or drop after verification)
    -- ALTER TABLE users DROP COLUMN full_name;

    RAISE NOTICE 'Migration completed: split full_name into first_name/last_name';
  ELSE
    RAISE NOTICE 'Migration already applied, skipping.';
  END IF;
END $$;

COMMIT;
```

**Rollback (undo):**
```sql
-- migration_001_split_name_rollback.sql

BEGIN;

DO $$
BEGIN
  IF EXISTS (
    SELECT 1 FROM information_schema.columns 
    WHERE table_name = 'users' AND column_name = 'first_name'
  ) THEN
    -- Restore full_name if dropped
    ALTER TABLE users ADD COLUMN full_name VARCHAR(255);
    UPDATE users SET full_name = TRIM(CONCAT(first_name, ' ', last_name));
    ALTER TABLE users ALTER COLUMN full_name SET NOT NULL;

    -- Drop new columns
    ALTER TABLE users DROP COLUMN first_name;
    ALTER TABLE users DROP COLUMN last_name;

    RAISE NOTICE 'Rollback completed: restored full_name, dropped first_name/last_name';
  ELSE
    RAISE NOTICE 'Columns already dropped or migration not applied.';
  END IF;
END $$;

COMMIT;
```

**Safety notes:**
- Wrapped in `BEGIN/COMMIT` — all-or-nothing
- `DO $$ IF NOT EXISTS $$` — re-runnable, safe on retry
- Split logic handles multi-word names (last space = split point) and single-word names
- Can run multiple times, skips if already done
- Backup `full_name` column before dropping (commented out — uncomment if needed)

Use: `psql -U user -d dbname -f migration_001_split_name.sql`
